> > Ok, This is a problem I always run into at Mines end.  I see 2 or 3 grey
> > stones and I have no idea which is a luckstone and which is not.  Normally I
> > kick the stones, but two of the 3 stones are up against a wall.  How do I
> > test grey stones that are up against a wall?
> 
> Dig out the wall?


Unless it's the gnome's wine cellar end, this won't work... non
diggable walls!  If there are 2 gray stones in a pile (2 gray stones,
not a gray stone and a gray stone), these are not luckstones.  In the
crypt end (with the level teleporters), there is a luckstone and a
flint stone on top of the level teleporters... neither is a loadstone.
 In the "original" minend level (with all the mimics), there should be
one luckstone and one loadstone.  Sadly, both are placed randomly with
one ruby and worthless piece of red glass.  If you cannot get to where
you can kick it, teleport it out and track it down.  Repeat until you
can kick-test it...

Other solutions:  curse test it with a pet.  Pick it up if you have a
scroll of remove curse, potion of holy water, or potion of polymorph
to burn.  Zap a wand of cancellation at it.  Stand on it if you are a
priest.  #praying should work if you are in good standing with your
deity, your prayer timeout has expired, and none of the following
apply:

Turning to stone
Turning to slime
Strangled
Stuck in lava
Deathly ill
Starving
Excessively low on HP
Lycanthropy
Collapsing (due to low capacity/heavy load due to diminished STR)
Stuck in a wall
Levitating due to cursed ring/boots
Unusable hands (cursed gloves, cursed 2 handed weapon, etc.)
Cursed blindfold/towel stuck to head
Punished with an iron ball
Wearing gauntlets/boots of fumbling

If all of these are not applicable, the worst_cursed_item function
first looks for a loadstone to uncurse (assuming you get a #prayer
benefit).

If all else fails, lug it around to exercise strength ;)

